 ### Added
 
+- **To-device messaging `PUT /_matrix/client/v3/sendToDevice/{eventType}/{txnId}` and `to_device.events` in `/sync` (story to-device-messaging, epic e2ee-client-support; migration 000059)**: device verification and key requests between devices work. Opaque per-device queue in `to_device_messages` / `to_device_txns` (never logged, deleted by the GDPR erasure), acknowledged by the `since` token of the next sync (retries redeliver), woken through `pg`. Recipients are the sender's own devices and users the sender shares a room with (otherwise silently skipped, no existence oracle); limits: 64 KiB body, 50 recipient entries, 500 messages / 8 MiB per device (oldest evicted), 7 days TTL, 60 requests per minute per user. Rooms stay unencrypted (ADR-011).
+
 - **Server-side key backup `/_matrix/client/v3/room_keys/**` (story server-side-key-backup, epic e2ee-client-support; migration 000058)**: Element's "chat recovery" and secret-storage bootstrap work. `POST|GET /room_keys/version`, `GET|PUT|DELETE /room_keys/version/{version}` and `PUT|GET|DELETE /room_keys/keys[/{roomId}[/{sessionId}]]` replace the former acceptance stub (a constant `200 {"version":"1"}` that stored nothing): an OPAQUE per-user store (tables `room_key_backup_versions` and `room_key_backup_sessions`; the server never decrypts or logs a blob, ADR-011 stays: no E2EE room is enabled), the spec's merge rule for a re-uploaded session, `etag` and `count` from the database, `403 M_WRONG_ROOM_KEYS_VERSION` with `current_version`, idempotent `DELETE` with a soft-delete marker (versions are never reused). Limits: 10 versions per user (the 11th is `403 M_FORBIDDEN`), 1000 version rows per user including the markers, 100 000 sessions per version, 8 KiB per `session_data`, 16 KiB per `auth_data`, 5 MiB per request body (read only after the authentication), a per-user storage budget of 64 MiB over all live versions (every session row costs its ids and 128 bytes besides its data; `403 M_FORBIDDEN`); writes are rate limited per user (60 per minute, burst 5), the two bulk reads (`GET /keys`, `GET /keys/{room}`) have their own bucket (30 per minute, burst 3) and at most one is in flight per user and two per node, `GET /version` has a light bucket (120 per minute, burst 30), a writer that finds the per-user lock busy answers `429 M_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` at once. The GDPR erasure deletes all versions and sessions of the user. Operators: run migration 000058 with the release; rolling back discards every user's key backup.
 
 - **`PUT /_matrix/client/v3/rooms/{roomId}/redact/{eventId}/{txnId}` and applied `m.room.redaction` events, audit action `room_event_redacted`, migration 000051 (story state-writer-redaction; follow-ups `fw`, `fv`, `fz`, `fx` closed)**: Element's "Remove" and "Remove recent messages" work. A redaction is decided and written by the room process (own event: `events["m.room.redaction"]`; another user's event: also the `redact` level), stored with a top-level `redacts` (new column `events.redacts`, migration 000051) and served with `redacts` and `content.redacts`; the redacted event is served pruned (`content: {}`, `unsigned.redacted_because`) on every read path while its content stays in the database (Compliance Mode); a redaction of another user's event writes the audit row `room_event_redacted`. Operator query **Q-rd** (07-deployment) lists legacy unchecked redactions.
diff --git a/docs/architecture/04-solution-strategy.md b/docs/architecture/04-solution-strategy.md
